     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "vo": "Why do a few kilometres matter? At one sixty, the ball reaches the batter in about four-tenths of a second. Every extra kilometre takes reaction time away.",
   "scene": {
    "type": "trajectory",
    "head": {
     "t": "THE 0.4-SECOND PROBLEM",
     "sub": "ILLUSTRATIVE · SIDE-ON"
    },
    "speed": "160 KM/H",
    "balls": [
     {
      "length": 6.0,
      "label": "0.4 SECONDS",
      "c": "red",
      "at": 0.15,
      "dur": 0.5
     }
    ],
    "note": "Release to batter at 160 km/h: about four-tenths of a second",
    "noteat": 0.4
   }
  },
  {
   "vo": "So why hasn't India produced a one-sixty bowler? For decades, Indian pitches rewarded spin and control, not raw speed. Coaching has valued line and length over chaos. And speed breaks bodies: both उमरान and मयंक have had their careers interrupted. The few express bowlers India finds are hard to protect.",
   "scene": {
    "type": "list",
    "head": {
     "t": "WHY NOT YET?"
    },
    "items": [
     {
      "h": "PITCHES BUILT FOR SPIN",
      "d": "Decades of surfaces that rewarded control, not speed",
      "at": 0.12
     },
     {
      "h": "CONTROL OVER CHAOS",
      "d": "Line and length valued over raw pace",
      "at": 0.35
     },
     {
      "h": "SPEED BREAKS BODIES",
      "d": "Umran's and Mayank's careers both interrupted",
      "c": "red",
      "at": 0.5
     },
     {
      "h": "HARD TO PROTECT",
      "d": "Few express bowlers, and fewer kept fit",
      "at": 0.8
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "vo": "But maybe India doesn't need it. जसप्रीत बुमराह rarely gets near one-fifty, and he's the best fast bowler in the world, with four for fifteen in a World Cup final this year. Skill beats speed.",
   "scene": {
    "type": "statement",
    "kicker": "THE COUNTER-ARGUMENT",
    "lines": [
     {
      "t": "SKILL"
     },
     {
      "t": "BEATS SPEED.",
      "c": "gold",
      "at": 0.4
     }
    ],
    "sub": "Exhibit A: Jasprit Bumrah, 4/15 in the 2026 T20 World Cup final",
    "subat": 0.55
   }
  },
  {
   "vo": "Our verdict? India's one-sixty is coming. Three Indian bowlers have now gone past one fifty-four in the IPL, and the pipeline has never been faster. The real question is whether the body can survive it.",
   "scene": {
    "type": "statement",
    "kicker": "OUR VERDICT",
    "lines": [
     {
      "t": "INDIA'S 160"
     },
     {
      "t": "IS COMING.",
